# Overview
#
# A fancy word stands in for a plainer one (`delve into` for `read`,
# `showcase` for `show`, `tapestry` for `mix`). The fancy word adds
# length and no meaning, and a reader who does not know it must look it
# up. Each word or phrase here turns up far more in generated text than
# in docs a person wrote. The fix writes the plain word. The rule sits
# at Recommended, because the plain word differs from word to word, and
# a name can hold one of the words.
#
# Expression
#
# `$foster`, `$showcase`, `$garner`, and `$boast` expand to every form
# of the word through Harper's dictionary. A space in a pattern is a
# whitespace token, so `deep[-, ( )]dive` lists a hyphen and a space.
# The pattern matches the spaced and the hyphenated spelling alike.
#
# `(landscape of)` does not open with `the`, so the branch also matches
# `the changing landscape of` and `a landscape of tools`.
#
# False Positives
#
# `unlock`, `harness`, `landscape`, `realm`, and `underscore` are left
# out, because each names something in code (a mutex, a test harness, a
# page orientation, a Kerberos realm, the character). The stock phrases
# built on them count instead (`harness the power`, `unlock the full
# potential`, `landscape of`, `the realm of`). `elevate privileges`
# names a security operation, so `elevate` skips a following
# `privilege`, `privileges`, or `permissions`.
#
# Related Rules
#
# The Required ProseFancyWord holds `utilize` and `leverage`, whose
# plain word is always `use`. The Recommended ProseFancyWord holds the
# words that turn up far more in generated text than in docs a person
# wrote. Their plain word differs from word to word. The Optional
# ProseFancyWord holds the words that human-written docs also use.
#
# ProseIdiom holds `under the hood`, `at its core`, and `strike a
# balance`, whose fix writes the literal meaning. ProseImportance holds
# `underscores the importance`.
#
# Measurement
#
# The rule hit 60 lines in the measure.py corpus, and 19 of 20 sampled
# hits stood in for a plainer word. The misfire was the name `Learning
# Journey Working Group`.
expr main [delve, delves, delving, (dive into), (deep[-, ( )]dive), unleash, unleashes, empower, empowers, empowering, streamline, streamlines, streamlined, ([elevate, elevates] ![privilege, privileges, permissions]), tapestry, journey, ([navigate, navigates, navigating] the [complexities, complexity, landscape, world, challenges]), testament, $foster, $showcase, $garner, $boast, interplay, intricacies, synergy, nuanced, multifaceted, meticulous, meticulously, bolster, bolsters, bolstered, bolstering, spearhead, spearheads, spearheaded, spearheading, supercharge, supercharges, supercharged, supercharging, revolutionize, revolutionizes, revolutionized, revolutionizing, embark, embarks, embarked, embarking, ([harness, harnesses, harnessing] the power), ([unlock, unlocks, unlocking] the potential), ([unlock, unlocks, unlocking] the [full, true] potential), (the realm of), (landscape of), (key takeaway), (key takeaways)]
let message "Fancy word. Use the plain word it stands for."
let description "Flags fancy words and phrases, such as `delve`, `showcase`, and `tapestry`, that stand in for a plainer word."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "Unlock releases the mutex."
allows "The test harness builds the fixture once."
allows "The realm names the Kerberos domain."
allows "Names with an underscore are private."
allows "The installer elevates privileges with sudo."
allows "The script elevates privilege for the install."
allows "Rotate the page to landscape orientation before printing."
